# {{name}}

{{description}}

A [QiForge](https://github.com/ixoworld/qiforge) oracle on Cloudflare Workers, built on [`@ixo/oracle-runtime-workers`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@ixo/oracle-runtime-workers). Scaffolded by `qiforge-cli new`.

## Requirements

- Node.js >= 22 and pnpm >= 10
- A Cloudflare account on the Workers Paid plan to deploy (local development needs no account)
- An `OPEN_ROUTER_API_KEY`

## Quickstart

```bash
pnpm install
# qiforge-cli new wrote .dev.vars; add your OPEN_ROUTER_API_KEY to it
# (scaffolded with --skip-entity? cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars and fill in
#  the identity vars in both wrangler configs first)
pnpm dev
curl http://localhost:8787/health
```

## Layout

```
src/
├── index.ts          # the oracle Worker — createOracleWorker + the Durable Object exports
├── gateway.ts        # the Matrix gateway Worker — createGatewayWorker
├── config.ts         # identity + prompt slots
├── config.test.ts    # the composed system prompt carries those slots
└── plugins/          # your plugins (qiforge-cli plugin new <name>)
test/                 # the test Worker the unit tests run in
wrangler.jsonc          # oracle script: vars, bindings, rate limit, crons
wrangler.gateway.jsonc  # gateway script
.dev.vars             # secrets for wrangler dev — never commit
oracle-credentials.env  # the oracle's wallet mnemonic and Matrix credentials — back up, never commit
```

## Scripts

| Command | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| `pnpm dev` | `wrangler dev` with both scripts on http://localhost:8787 |
| `pnpm test` | Unit tests inside workerd (`@cloudflare/vitest-plugin`) |
| `pnpm typecheck` | Type-check without emitting |
| `pnpm run build` | `wrangler deploy --dry-run` for both scripts (bundles into `dist/`) |
| `pnpm run deploy` | Deploy the gateway script, then the oracle script |
| `pnpm cf-typegen` | Generate `worker-configuration.d.ts` from `wrangler.jsonc` |

## Deploy

```bash
pnpm exec wrangler login
pnpm run deploy
pnpm exec wrangler secret bulk .dev.vars                                   # oracle script
pnpm exec wrangler secret put MATRIX_ORACLE_ADMIN_PASSWORD -c wrangler.gateway.jsonc
pnpm exec wrangler secret put MATRIX_RECOVERY_PHRASE -c wrangler.gateway.jsonc
pnpm exec wrangler secret put MATRIX_VALUE_PIN -c wrangler.gateway.jsonc
qiforge-cli update-oracle-api-url                                          # point the entity at the deployed URL
```

Both wrangler configs set `"minify": true`: the minified bundle leaves the user objects far more of their 128 MB isolate heap. Keep it on.

## Adding a plugin

```bash
qiforge-cli plugin new my-plugin
```

Scaffolds `src/plugins/my-plugin/` with a sample tool and tests. Register it in `src/index.ts`:

```ts
import { MyPluginPlugin } from './plugins/my-plugin/my-plugin.plugin';

const oracle = createOracleWorker({
  config,
  plugins: [...BUNDLED_WORKERS_PLUGINS, new MyPluginPlugin()],
});
```

## Upgrading the runtime

Bump `@ixo/oracle-runtime-workers` and set `@ixo/matrix-bot-workers-sdk` to the exact version that release depends on (`npm view @ixo/oracle-runtime-workers@<version> dependencies`), then `pnpm install && pnpm typecheck && pnpm test && pnpm run build`.
